@page /islands
@mode SSG
@tag home

<div class="page-intro"><a class="breadcrumb" href="../">← OVERVIEW</a><p class="eyebrow">VOLT.NET / ISLAND LAB</p><h1>One island.<br />A typed server action.</h1><p class="lead">The surrounding page is HTML. The Counter carries serialized state; a C# action returns new state, and the server renders the next fragment.</p></div>
<div class="notice"><strong>Hosting boundary:</strong> this GitHub Pages deployment is static. The Counter below is a server-rendered preview, not an interactive JavaScript copy. Run the demo locally to use the real action endpoint.</div>
<div class="demo-grid"><div class="specimen"><div class="panel-label"><span>COMPONENT</span><span>Components/Counter.cs · excerpt</span></div><pre><code>@("public sealed record CounterState(int Count);\n\n[VoltIsland]\npublic sealed partial class Counter\n    : VoltComponent<CounterState>\n{\n    [VoltAction]\n    public static CounterState Increment(\n        CounterState state,\n        System.Text.Json.JsonElement args)\n        => state with { Count = state.Count + 1 };\n\n    // Render uses State.Count and a submit button:\n    // Name(\"__volt_action\"), Value(\"increment\"),\n    // DataVoltOn(\"click:increment\")\n}")</code></pre><div class="panel-label"><span>TEMPLATE</span><span>Counter partial</span></div><pre><code>@("<volt-island name=\"Counter\"\n    state='{\"count\":0}' />")</code></pre></div><div><div class="specimen"><div class="panel-label"><span>REAL COMPONENT OUTPUT</span><span>Static during export</span></div><div class="preview">@Counter("Counter / initial state")</div></div><div class="notice"><strong>Local mode:</strong> JavaScript enabled → POST to <code>/_volt/action</code> and fragment replacement. JavaScript disabled → ordinary form POST to <code>/_volt/fallback</code> and redirect. Both execute C# on the server.</div></div></div>
<section class="demo-section"><p class="eyebrow">RUN IT / NO SIMULATION</p><h2>Try the actual round trip.</h2><pre><code>@("git clone https://github.com/Puxxalwl/Volt.NET.git\ncd Volt.NET/apps/demo\nDOTNET_ROLL_FORWARD=Major dotnet run -c Release -- --port 5000\n\n# Open http://localhost:5000/islands/")</code></pre><p class="small">Install the SDK pinned by the repository first. In local mode the same Counter button is enabled. Disable JavaScript to inspect the form fallback.</p><div class="flow"><span>click:increment</span><span>→ typed C# action</span><span>→ new CounterState</span><span>→ HTML fragment</span></div></section>
<section class="demo-section"><p class="eyebrow">WASM / EXPERIMENTAL</p><h2>A protocol, not automatic C# compilation.</h2><p>Volt also has an experimental WebAssembly island contract. A compatible module must export memory, alloc, volt_dispatch and volt_render. The hydration runtime can call it without a server round trip.</p><p>The repository tests that protocol with a fixture module. This C# Counter has no WASM module, so exporting it does not make its C# action run in the browser.</p><p><a class="copy-link" href="https://github.com/Puxxalwl/Volt.NET/blob/main/CONTRACT.md">Read the island & WASM contract ↗</a></p></section>
